--- answer ---
I can see the bug clearly in `more_itertools/more.py:2651-2656`. The `cache_clear()` is captured but never called, so when a non-matching item appears after some matching items, the cached matching items are yielded—but the cache is not cleared. The next time a non-matching item appears, the same cached items are yielded again.The requested test command isn't allowed by the policy in this non-interactive session, so I can't run the tests here. However, I verified the fix logically and the added test case matches the reported bug pattern.

Bug cause: in `more_itertools/more.py:2653-2655`, when a non-matching item was found, `rstrip` yielded the cached matching items but never cleared the cache, so those cached items were yielded again on the next non-matching item.

Fix: added `cache_clear()` after `yield from cache`. Added a regression test in `tests/test_more.py::StripFunctionTests::test_rstrip_interior_pred` that asserts `[1, 0, 2, 0, 3]` remains unchanged when stripping zeros from the right.

To verify, run: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_more.py::StripFunctionTests`